# InterMUN Intentional UI Rule

Use this theme as the source of truth for **all** UI (landing, app chrome, documents, prototypes). Designs should feel human, slightly imperfect, and emotionally engaging — not templated.

## Color & Tone
- Background base: pastel blue `#DFF2FC`
- Anchor with one strong neutral; text contrast ≥ 4.5:1
- Soft gradients/shadows only to draw attention — never everywhere
- No neon, glow-everywhere accents, or oversaturated palettes

## Typography
- Distinct heading font (e.g. Clash Display) + clean body (e.g. Inter Tight / Satoshi)
- Mix weights and letter-spacing; 2–3 natural heading scales
- Avoid Poppins + Inter + Manrope and single-weight sites
- No oversized hero text without visual balance

## Layout & Composition
- Prefer asymmetry / staggered sections; vary composition between sections
- Intentional whitespace — not equal gaps everywhere
- Break the grid slightly (offset a card, pull a button toward its title)
- Alternate background tones or padding for rhythm
- Never clone identical section structures back-to-back

## Buttons & Microcopy
- One primary + one secondary button style
- Descriptive CTAs (“Start studying free”), not “Get started”
- Conversational copy; no “Unlock your potential” / “Empower your future”
- Subtle hover (lift, soft color shift); no harsh shadows or glowing edges

## Cards & Components
- Vary card heights slightly; hero radius ~16px, small cards ~8–10px
- Soft shadows or pastel borders for depth
- Keep existing component naming/IA intact (Sidebar, Top Bar, Cards, Documents, Voting, Chair Controls, etc.)
- Enhance only via color, texture, motion — do not change labels or structural naming

## Visuals & Motion
- Mix illustrations with at least one real photo; consistent illustration style
- Tiny hand-drawn accents / doodles welcome; no generic 3D blobs
- Motion 300–500ms with varied direction/delay per section — not identical sync fades

## Polish Checklist
- Contrast passes; no repeated section pattern twice in a row
- Hierarchy feels natural; hover states vary slightly across CTAs
- At least one cue (photo, doodle, quote) that feels real
